            "review_title": "Review at Hong Kong Sheng Kee Dessert",
            "review_text": "maryyeo\nHo Chi Minh City, Vietnam4531 contributions\n0\nDim Sum cafe chain that serves my familiar comfort Chinese dishes\nMay 2020\nA popular Hong Kong cafe chain that started in Singapore, and just opened in Vietnam, among many other overseas outlets.\n\nIt serves up all the comfort Hong Kong style Chinese foods such as:\n- Noodles or Rice with Wanton/ Char Siew/ Braised Chicken/ Pork\n- Congees/ Porridges with seafood, sliced fish or preserved egg and pork ball\n- Dim Sum dishes such as - Siew Mai, Har Gao, Char Siew Buns, etc.\n- Various desserts such as - Chilled Mango Sago & Pomelo Dessert (杨枝甘露)\n\nThe small outlet that is styled as just one of the cafes within the mall's basement, with a modest number of 12 tables or so, makes it a perfect spot for casual and inexpensive yet satisfying dining/snacking/chilling spot.\n\nI won't say it's the most authentic Chinese/Hong Kong food I've ever tasted in Vietnam, nor does it have a huge variety of dishes to choose from, but if you're missing decent Hong Kong/ Chinese food that is affordable (e.g. ~usd4 for a main dish of rice/noodles) and has all the favourite hits, this is the place to go. I just hope the signature HK Milk Tea can be more dense.. it tasted a tad too diluted.\nRead more\nValue\nService\nFood\nReview collected in partnership with this restaurant \nWritten August 11, 2020",
